## Findings and fixes (both in 1145e2054, gate script only; no app code change)

- F370 [Nit] FIX. Cause: the turn 14 note claimed recorded `<audio controls>` speakers sit
  in the scrolling parent block by design; that is wrong for the week tiles — `TileCard`
  renders a child-facing label Speaker inside each tile `li`, in the same landscape row as
  the tile links, and no row measured it. Fix: the gate function
  `allControlsAtLandscape` gains an `extraSelector` probe, and `all_controls_visible_week`
  measures `[data-week-tiles] audio` on the bottom and the right edge, printing
  `speakers_found`, `speakers_outside`, and `speaker_bottom_px`; a speaker outside the
  viewport fails the row. Measured today: `speakers_found=0, speaker_bottom_px=0` — no
  tile recording ships yet (`TILE_LABEL_AUDIO` is empty), so no defect is shown and no app
  code change was needed. The plan Turn 14 block holds a `Correction (turn 15, F370):`
  line instead of a history rewrite.
- F371 [Nit] FIX. Cause: each `all_controls_visible` row passed on `count > 0 &&
  outside === 0`, so a screen that fell back to the week-home link (a missing book or a
  missing song) would pass with one link inside the viewport (A4 class). Fix: each row
  holds a per-screen minimum count from the measured values with `>=` — week 3, reader 9,
  end of book 3, decodable 8, song 1, question 4 — and prints `controls_min`. Fail-first
  proof: the `/one-link` self-test page (one link inside the viewport) is measured by the
  same function in one run, which prints `old_rule_passes=true new_rule_passes=false
  (controls_found=1, controls_min=9)` — the old `count > 0` rule improperly passed the
  page and the new reader minimum rejects it. The self-test loop accepts the page only
  when the new rule fails, so the row is not vacuous.

